<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Portugal Cove-St. Philip's is a town of steep driveways, big rural lots and older homes that still heat with oil. Whether you're above the ferry terminal in Portugal Cove, out along St. Thomas Line, or down a lane in St. Philip's, there's a fair chance your tank sits outside on a slope taking the full force of the wind off Conception Bay. That's the kind of setup that ages a steel tank faster than the date on the tag suggests.</p><p>Harbour Tank Co handles <a href="/oil-tank-replacement-st-johns/">oil tank replacement</a>, <a href="/oil-tank-removal-st-johns/">removal</a> and <a href="/fibreglass-oil-tank-upgrade-st-johns/">fibreglass upgrades</a> across the whole town, from Beachy Cove and Portugal Cove to Hogan's Pond, St. Thomas and St. Philip's. Every job starts with a free written estimate, and removal of the old tank is included with every replacement. If your HOST tag has expired or the delivery truck has just turned around in your driveway, our <a href="/expired-oil-tank-emergency-st-johns/">24/7 emergency line</a> at (709) 800-3117 is there for exactly that.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Portugal Cove-St. Philip's</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Portugal Cove-St. Philip's Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Oil Tank Replacement</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">New 200-gallon steel or fibreglass tanks installed on sloped lots and in basements across Portugal Cove-St. Philip's, with the old tank hauled away on the same visit. Painted steel is $3,200 installed and fibreglass is $3,850, and both prices include removal of the old tank.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Oil Tank Removal and Disposal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Once a tank is disconnected, NL regulations give you 30 days to empty it, remove it and restore the site. Outdoor tank removal is $500, and basement removals in the older homes around Portugal Cove and St. Philip's are quoted case by case.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Fibreglass Tank Upgrade</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Salt air off the Tickle and freeze-thaw on a hillside are hard on steel. A fibreglass tank doesn't rust, and its registration can run for decades instead of the 10 to 20 years an outdoor steel tank is allowed.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Expired Tag and Leak Emergencies</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Refused a delivery in January with the wind howling in off the bay? Call our 24/7 line and we'll get an installer to your door and a new tag on the system as fast as the road up to your place allows.</p>
      </div>
</div>
